  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Decision\\n\\n**The ordering guarantee that applies to the integration represented by this workspace is the *durable per-ledger commit-observation order* of committed management-state revisions** — the position sequence `change_seq` exposed by `StateChangeFeed.changes()` (ORD-BOOT-0 §3, registered as SCF-INV-1…7 and hardened by ORD-BOOT-0.1 as SCF-INV-8…10).\\n\\nIt is a strictly increasing, never-reused, per-database total order over *commits*, assigned by the storage engine inside the same transaction that commits the revision. It is explicitly **not** a causal order, **not** a wall-clock order, **not** a business-priority order, and **not** an order across separate ledgers, hosts or machines.\\n\\n## What \\\"the integration\\\" is here\\n\\nThis workspace (Ordarium) participates in the Ordarium ↔ Palimpsest integration through two seams:\\n\\n| Seam | Carrier | Ordering guarantee |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Host invocation (`HostInvocationPort`, G18 `@ordarium/host-kit`) | version handshake `HOST_CONTRACT_VERSION = 1`, port mapping, conformance runner | **None** — no ordering contract at all |\\n| Revisioned state observation (`StateChangeFeed`, ORD-BOOT-0/0.1) | `changes(filter?, cursor?)` over t",
